    <h3>Processing</h3>
    <p>A very broad term covering <em>any</em> operation performed on personal data: collection, storage, use, sharing, disclosure, deletion, or destruction — whether automated or manual.</p>

    <h3>Consent Manager</h3>
    <p>A new role introduced by the DPDP Act — a registered entity that acts as a single platform through which a Data Principal can give, manage, review, and withdraw consent for multiple Data Fiduciaries. Think of it as a <em>central dashboard</em> for all your data consents.</p>

    <div class="callout">
      <div class="callout-label">Key Insight</div>
      <p>The DPDP Act is <strong>purpose-limitation focused</strong>. Data collected for one purpose cannot simply be used for another without fresh consent. If a bank collects your data to open a savings account, it cannot use that data to sell you insurance without your fresh, specific consent.</p>
    </div>
