    <p>The government retains significant power here — it can restrict transfers to specific countries for reasons of <strong>national security, sovereignty, or foreign policy</strong>. This gives India strategic flexibility in data diplomacy while still enabling global business operations.</p>

    <div class="callout warning">
      <div class="callout-label">Business Impact</div>
      <p>Global companies operating in India (like Google, Meta, or Amazon) must closely monitor the whitelist notifications. Transferring Indian users' data to a non-whitelisted jurisdiction — even inadvertently through cloud routing — could attract penalties. Legal and compliance teams must map all data flows and update contracts accordingly.</p>
