  <section class="section" id="s10">
    <h2>10. Types of Intermediaries &amp; Their Obligations</h2>

    <h3>Category 1 — All Intermediaries (Baseline Obligations)</h3>
    <p>Every intermediary operating in India, regardless of size, must:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Publish its <strong>Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, and User Agreement</strong> in English and the regional language of the relevant State.</li>
      <li>Inform users of prohibited content categories and consequences of violations.</li>
      <li><strong>Not host</strong> content that is obscene, defamatory, threatens national security, incites communal violence, or violates the IT Act or other laws.</li>
      <li>Appoint a <strong>Grievance Officer</strong> — an Indian resident who must acknowledge complaints within 24 hours and resolve them within 15 days.</li>
      <li>Remove or disable access to unlawful content within <strong>36 hours</strong> of receiving government/court orders.</li>
      <li><strong>Preserve records</strong> of users for 180 days (for law enforcement cooperation).</li>
    </ul>

