    <h3>Compliance Challenge for Platforms</h3>
    <p>For a large platform like Meta (operating Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp in India), compliance now involves:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Maintaining a <strong>Data Protection Officer</strong> (if designated Significant Data Fiduciary under DPDP)</li>
      <li>Maintaining a <strong>Chief Compliance Officer</strong> and <strong>Nodal Officer</strong> (under IT Rules as SSMI)</li>
      <li>Running a <strong>Consent Manager</strong> compatible consent interface (DPDP)</li>
      <li>Operating a <strong>Grievance Appellate Committee</strong> interface (IT Rules)</li>
      <li>Publishing a <strong>monthly compliance report</strong> (IT Rules)</li>
      <li>Conducting <strong>Data Protection Impact Assessments</strong> (DPDP for SDFs)</li>
      <li>Enabling <strong>first-originator traceability</strong> for WhatsApp (IT Rules) — while maintaining end-to-end encryption</li>
    </ul>
